bservation that summability still follows does not diagnose the malformed theorem item.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]},{"gold_issue_id":"2510.24544:I005","focus_prediction_issue_id":"ISSUE-002","focus_relation":"different_obligation_or_hypothesis","gold_causal_unit_ids":["2510.24544:I005:U001","2510.24544:I005:U002","2510.24544:I005:U003","2510.24544:I005:U005"],"prediction_causal_unit_ids":["ISSUE-002:U003","ISSUE-002:U005","ISSUE-002:U006","ISSUE-002:U008"],"same_causal_subject":false,"same_failed_obligation":false,"same_failure_operation":false,"identity_explanation":"The gold issue is the unsupported inference from finite plotted partial sums to convergence of an infinite series and hence to a rate guarantee. ISSUE-002 identifies a separate parameter-regime failure of averagedness in the matrix-completion operator; it does not diagnose the finite-prefix-versus-infinite-tail evidentiary gap.","shared_mathematical_weakness":"","uncovered_gold_detail":"","coverage_status":"not_matched","supporting_prediction_issue_ids":[],"combination_explanation":"","component_coverage":[]}],"audit":{"all_gold_ids_decided":true,"all_ranked_candidates_considered":true,"target_type_not_used_for_identity":true,"severity_not_used_for_identity":true,"prediction_reuse_requires_explicit_issue_support":true,"each_gold_credited_at_most_once":true,"combined_entries_are_self_contained_diagnoses":true,"support_limit_three_respected":true}}